      "source": "execution",
      "review_round": null,
      "summary": "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/kernel/capability_registry.ts:66 stores the caller's mutable binding object by reference, whereas both prior registries snapshotted it; mutating task, digest, expiry, or other fields after issue can rebind an existing capability, so store a shallow copy of the validated binding."
    },
    {
      "id": "review-2",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "acc-2",
      "source": "execution",
      "review_round": null,
      "summary": "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/kernel/authority_port.ts:156 binds consume directly to the inner registry, bypassing the adapter's opaque-capability error normalization, so fabricated or cross-registry consume calls expose a different error than before; wrap or normalize consume through the mutation adapter."
    }
  ],
